{
  "kanji": "向",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 向\ntitle: face toward\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 6\nradical: 口\nradicalNumber: 30\nonyomi: [コウ]\nkunyomi: [む.く, む.い, -む.き, む.ける, -む.け, む.かう, む.かい, む.こう, む.こう-, むこ, むか.い]\ndistractors: [同, 問, 何]\n---\n\n# 向 — face toward\n\n**Strokes:** 6 · **Key (radical):** 口 (no. 30) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n向 concerns orientation: which way something faces or heads.\n[向く](../words/向く.md) むく describes turning or facing, while 向かう むかう can describe heading toward a destination.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine looking through the inner 口 opening in one direction.\nThis is a picture suggested by the modern shape, not an account of its origin.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| む.く | kun | [向く](../words/向く.md) むく — turn toward; face |\n| む.かう | kun | 向かう むかう — head toward |\n| コウ | on | 方向 ほうこう — direction |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [向く](../words/向く.md) むく — face; turn toward\n- 向ける むける — direct; turn something toward\n- 向かう むかう — head toward\n- 方向 ほうこう — direction; orientation\n\n## Notes\n\n右を向く (みぎをむく) means \"turn to the right\"; it does not by itself mean traveling rightward.\nCompare [同](同.md): 向 has a short slanting stroke above its outer frame, rather than 同's inner horizontal line.\nThe other source readings are retained in metadata.\n\nSources: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project);\n[JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1277080, 1277100, 1604800, 1516990.\n",
